// cffi U4 — VARARGS, arm 2: `fcntl(fd, F_GETFL, 0)` — the shape the effect-loop
// port actually needs (`effectloop.zig:117` declares `fcntl(c_int, c_int, ...)
// -> c_int`).
//
// WHY THIS ARM EXISTS BESIDES snprintf: snprintf is a variadic call whose extra
// arguments are all IMMEDIATES, so a lowering that dropped them entirely would
// still pass a "did the format print" test only if the format had no
// conversions.  Here the variadic argument is a real argument to a real libc
// entry point, and the RESULT depends on the call succeeding: `F_GETFL` (3) on
// fd 1 returns the file-status flags, which are non-negative.  A call emitted
// without the third argument (or with the argument in the wrong class) can
// still return >= 0 — so, stated plainly: the golden's discriminating power is
// on the CALL ARRIVING, and the STRUCTURAL pin
// (`=w call $fcntl(w 1, w 3, ..., l 0)` + `extsw`) is what holds the classes
// (`w` for the two C `int` parameters, `l` for the word-class variadic one) and
// the marker's position.
module Ffic
export Ffic.flags : val -> val

extern fcntl(fd : i32, cmd : i32, ...) -> i32;

defun Ffic.flags(dummy : val) -> val {
  word r = rawcall fcntl(1, 3, 0);
  return mkbool(r >= 0);
}
